# roam-323: the Settings > System per-profile proxy section — the upstream MOUNT only. All
# logic is additive //roamux: the pure validator/builder (//roamux/browser/proxy) and the
# settings handler (//roamux/browser/ui/webui/roamux_proxy_handler), the roam-13
# shortcuts-handler precedent. Chromium ships the whole proxy engine and no UI for it on macOS;
# this patch adds the seam, not the engine. No //net patch and no prefs_util.cc patch: `proxy`
# is already allowlisted as a dictionary for the settings API.
#
# Gated by roamux::features::kRoamuxProxyConfig, which ships DISABLED (the chrome://flags row
# lives in patch 0073, the sole owner of the three flag files). With the flag off the page keeps
# upstream's stock "open your computer's proxy settings" row untouched; roam-326 owns graduation.
#
# Files: chrome/browser/BUILD.gn (handler sources + the //roamux/browser/proxy dep),
# chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_ui.cc (handler registration),
# chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_localized_strings_provider.cc (the section's strings
# and the roamuxProxyConfigEnabled gate), chrome/browser/resources/settings/BUILD.gn (the
# component in web_component_files), system_page/system_page.{html,ts} (mount + import + gate)
# and the new system_page/roamux_proxy_section.{html,ts}.
#
# ORDERING DEPENDENCIES (shared-file successor protocol): after 0011 and 0033 for
# settings_ui.cc; after 0050 for chrome/browser/BUILD.gn; after 0070 for
# settings_localized_strings_provider.cc; after 0033 for resources/settings/BUILD.gn. Its number
# (0076) keeps it last, so a rebase of any of those re-verifies this patch.
#
# RETIREMENT: when upstream ships its own in-browser proxy configuration for macOS, retire this
# patch and the feature rather than stacking two editors; at every uprev re-check
# system_page.{html,ts} for an upstream proxy editor and prefs_util.cc for the allowlist rows.
#
# Regression: roamux_unittests ProxyConfigBuilderTest.*; roamux_browsertests
# RoamuxProxy*Test.* (handler guards, routing/precedence, and the settings DOM).
